@startuml
actor User
participant FE
participant BE
participant DB

User -> FE : Upload edited file\n+ own password\n(must be owner or shared user with can_edit)

FE -> BE : PUT /files/{id}\n(new file bytes, password, enc_algo, hash_algo)\n[multipart/form-data, JWT in header]

BE -> BE : Validate JWT

BE -> DB : Fetch file record
DB --> BE : file record

BE -> DB : Check access:\nowner OR share with can_edit=true AND not expired
DB --> BE : access result

alt no access or expired
    BE --> FE : 403 Forbidden
    FE --> User : Error — edit permission denied
else access granted

    BE -> DB : Fetch caller encrypted private key\n(private_key_enc, salt, nonce)
    DB --> BE : encrypted private key blob

    BE -> BE : Derive AES key from password\n(PBKDF2 + stored salt)
    BE -> BE : Decrypt private key blob\n→ RSA private key object

    BE -> BE : Unwrap caller's FEK copy\nusing RSA private key (access proof)

    BE -> BE : Compute new hash of new plaintext\n(SHA-256 / SHA-512 / MD5)\nbefore encryption

    BE -> BE : Generate new random FEK\n(32 bytes via os.urandom)\nOld FEK is discarded

    BE -> BE : Generate new random nonce / IV
    BE -> BE : Encrypt new file using new FEK + nonce\n→ new ciphertext\n(AES-256-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305)

    BE -> DB : Fetch owner public key PEM
    DB --> BE : owner public_key_pem

    BE -> BE : Wrap new FEK for owner\n(RSA-OAEP with owner public key)

    BE -> DB : Fetch all share recipients for this file
    DB --> BE : [{ recipient_id, public_key_pem }, ...]

    BE -> BE : Wrap new FEK for each recipient\n(RSA-OAEP with each recipient public key)

    BE -> DB : UPDATE file record\n(ciphertext, nonce, file_hash,\nenc_algo, hash_algo, wrapped_fek_owner)
    BE -> DB : UPDATE each share record\n(new wrapped_fek per recipient)
    DB --> BE : OK

    BE --> FE : 200 OK\n{ file_id, filename, file_hash, enc_algo, hash_algo }
    FE --> User : File updated successfully

end
@enduml
